{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgfxUVcb3sSS3ktqU8E3K","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fitting the three bands with a full d⁶ ligand-field calculation gives **Dq ≈ 1 860 cm⁻¹** and **B ≈ 810 cm⁻¹**. I did the fit numerically, not with a closed-form expression.\n\n**Method.**\n- I built the full d⁶ Hamiltonian in an octahedral field (orbital splitting 10Dq) with the Coulomb interaction written in terms of the Racah parameters B and C. C was tied to B by C = 4B.\n- I diagonalised it in the M_S = 0 determinant space and kept only the S = 0 states, which I picked out by their ⟨S²⟩ value.\n- From the ¹A₁g ground state, the spin-allowed bands go to triply degenerate singlets (¹T₁g and ¹T₂g). I took the three lowest triply degenerate singlet levels, measured from the ground state, as the model's three bands.\n- I then varied Dq and B to match 16 700, 26 330 and 35 020 cm⁻¹ by least squares.\n\n**Result.** The best fit is Dq ≈ 1 856 cm⁻¹, B ≈ 811 cm⁻¹ and C = 4B ≈ 3 244 cm⁻¹. The fitted bands come out at about 16 750, 26 345 and 34 980 cm⁻¹. These miss the observed bands by roughly 54, 15 and 37 cm⁻¹.\n\nTwo parameters are fitted to three bands, so the fit is overdetermined and the small residuals are expected. B is about 75% of a typical free-ion value for Co³⁺ (roughly 1 100 cm⁻¹), which is plausible for a covalent low-spin complex.\n\n{\"Dq\": 1856, \"B\": 811, \"C\": 3244, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Least-squares fit of the full d6 low-spin ligand-field (Tanabe-Sugano-type) model with C/B=4 to the three singlet-singlet bands.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2753,"cache_read_input_tokens":4924,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2753,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transform